## Want to Help?

Early boot, PE loading, XMem, and basic D3D12 plumbing are already working here. Whether you are a **human developer** or an **AI coding agent**, jump straight into these **high-impact, often-untouched areas** that directly unlock visible frames, live audio, fast shader builds, and hardware fidelity:

### A. First Visible Frame on Vulkan (`runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp`, `runtime/shims/d3d12_vulkan_device.cpp`, `runtime/src/vulkan_replay.h`)
- **Clear the remaining v10 view warnings**: console format casting for BCn/R8/R16/R32 views, MSAA typeless colour SRVs, and non-UAV texture UAV requests.
- **Wire UI colour blending**: hook the already-tested `runtime/shims/cb_blend_decode.h` (`CB_BLENDn_CONTROL` state block) into device slot-57 pipeline creation so UI alpha blending renders instead of forcing opaque pipelines.
- **Guest descriptor materializer & automatic RT→SRV barriers**: mirror guest-backed >1M descriptor heaps into the Vulkan bindless set and track render-target-to-SRV transitions across `FlushGpuCachesX`.
- **Persistent Vulkan pipeline cache**: wire the already-tested `runtime/src/pipeline_cache_store.h` into `runtime/shims/d3d12_vulkan_device.cpp` for sub-second repeat Vulkan startup.

### B. Real-Time Audio Output & Mixing (`runtime/shims/audio_x.cpp`, `runtime/shims/acphal.cpp`, `runtime/src/opus_mft_decoder.h`, `runtime/src/xma2_decoder.cpp`)
- Rarely touched by other forks — both the native Windows 11 Opus MFT decoder and the portable XMA2/WMA-Pro decoder already compile and pass tests.
- **Wire a low-latency Windows WASAPI render sink** (with an opt-in headless mute flag for CI).
- **Implement real multi-channel voice mixing** (gain, pitch resampling, stereo panning) in `chad.dll`, and stress-test multi-stream XMA2 packet ring wraparound and loop-point transitions.

### C. Rust-Accelerating `rdna2spirv` Hot Loops (`tools/rdna2spirv.py`, `tools/native/`)
- SPIR-V assembly (`spirv_asm_native`, `42×`) and RDNA2 disassembly (`rdna2_decode_native`) are already native Rust.
- The **#1 remaining CPU bottleneck** on giant 3–7 MB mesh shaders is pure Python CFG structuring, register liveness, and VGPR/SGPR value forwarding in `tools/rdna2spirv.py` — porting those hot passes into `tools/native/` will cut full-corpus shader translation from ~45 minutes to seconds.

### D. Vulkan Ray Tracing (XDXR / `VK_KHR_acceleration_structure`) & Shader Conformance
- **End-to-end live BLAS/TLAS build + trace validation** with colliding low-40-bit guest virtual addresses (`runtime/shims/xbox_bvh_builder.cpp`, `runtime/src/xdxr_build.h`).
- **Structural `spirv_opt` passes** for heavy RT and compute shaders so complex modules compile quickly on NVIDIA/AMD Vulkan drivers.
- **Wave64 cross-half VS/PS/GS correctness** on 32-wide subgroups (NVIDIA/Intel) and new hand-written GPU readback tests under `runtime/test/shaders/`.

### E. DirectStorage / BCPack Streaming & Console ABI Tail
- **Remaining BCPack BC6H/BC7 decompression calibration** (`tools/bcpack.py`, `runtime/src/bcpack_dstorage.cpp`).
- **Unmapped console command-list slots past frame #1** (auditing shifted PC slots vs console-only commands).
- **Automated pixel-ratio visual regression check** via `runtime/src/present_dump.h` (strictly aggregate non-zero pixel ratios / colour counts, zero screenshots committed) and **FidelityFX FSR upscaler integration**.

### F. Assets, World & Map Viewer (`tools/`, `viewer/`, `runtime/test/`)
- Investigate the remaining unrecovered model fragments in `levels.rpf` ([docs/models.md](docs/models.md#full-archive-re-count-at-e293917)).
- Build animation, physics, and world/map viewer features (`viewer/`), or expand standalone C++ and Python semantic/unit tests (**zero game files needed**).

### Contributor & AI Agent Guides
- **[docs/DEV_FRONTIERS.md](docs/DEV_FRONTIERS.md)** — detailed task breakdowns, ready-to-wire headers, and exact file pointers.
- **[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md)** & **[docs/CONTRIBUTING_ULTIMATE.md](docs/CONTRIBUTING_ULTIMATE.md)** — local build, testing, and PR workflow.
- **[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)** — rules for AI coding agents working on this codebase, including three hard constraints:
  1. **No non-trivial `thread_local` in `gta6rt.exe`** (conflicts with guest TLS on Windows and triggers `0xC0000409` aborts — use a thread-ID map instead).
  2. **Zero game data, ever** (`python -I scripts/check_no_game_data.py`).
  3. **Strict license wall** (GPL-3.0 or clean-room MIT/Apache-2.0 ports with attribution in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) only; never copy from GPL-2.0 or unlicensed repos).

