## How to Build

### 1. Developer / Contributor Build (No Game Files Needed)

Prerequisites: **Windows 10/11 x64**, Visual Studio 2022/2026 C++20 x64 toolset + Windows SDK 10.0.26100+, CMake + Ninja, [Vulkan SDK](https://vulkan.lunarg.com/) (headers >= 1.3.294), Python 3.12+, and [Rust (`cargo`)](https://rustup.rs/) for the 8 native accelerator DLLs.

```powershell
git clone --recursive <this-repo-url>
cd leonida-ultimate

# Build the Windows runtime & run CTests (from a Visual Studio Developer PowerShell):
cmake -S runtime -B runtime/build -G Ninja `
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DLEONIDA_BUILD_WINDOWS_RUNTIME=ON `
  -DCMAKE_POLICY_DEFAULT_CMP0141=NEW -DCMAKE_MSVC_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT=Embedded
cmake --build runtime/build --target gta6rt -j 8
ctest --test-dir runtime/build --output-on-failure --no-tests=error

# Build & test all 8 zero-dependency Rust accelerators (~4s):
cargo build --release --workspace --manifest-path tools/native/Cargo.toml
cargo test  --release --workspace --manifest-path tools/native/Cargo.toml

# Run translator semantic tests, unit tests, and the zero-game-data check:
python -I scripts/run_semantic_tests.py tests/semantic
python -I scripts/check_no_game_data.py
```

### 2. End-User Build From Your Own Copy (`make_game.py`)

Additional prerequisites for a full build from your Xbox Series 1.0.2.1 package: [.NET 8 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/8.0), [LLVM 21+](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases) with the **AMDGPU target** (`LLVM_MC`; see `scripts\build_llvm_mc.ps1` or `conda install -c conda-forge llvm-tools`), and optional `ffmpeg` on PATH.

```powershell
python -I make_game.py --find
python -I make_game.py --check
python -I make_game.py --game "D:\path\to\your\package" --out "D:\Games\Leonida" --work "E:\leonida-work"
python -I make_game.py --stages check,shaders,runtime   # ~30 GB instead of ~400 GB full asset export
python -I make_game.py --stages check,shaders,runtime --wave64-emulate auto --assembler auto --no-validate
```

Key runtime environment variables (see [ULTIMATE.md](ULTIMATE.md) and [docs/d3d12_vulkan.md](docs/d3d12_vulkan.md) for the full list):
- `LEONIDA_SHADERS=<path>` — directory of translated SPIR-V shaders and `index.json`.
- `LEONIDA_LAZY_PSO=1` — defer Vulkan PSO compilation until first draw/dispatch use.
- `LEONIDA_JIT_SHADERS=<cache_dir>` — opt-in warm on-demand JIT shader translation daemon when a prebuilt shader corpus is absent or incomplete.
- `LEONIDA_ARENA_MB=4096` — size of the console GPU address arena in MiB.
- `LEONIDA_RT_AS=khr` — use `VK_KHR_acceleration_structure` instead of the default software XDXR BVH4 layout (`off` disables RT AS on low-VRAM GPUs).

Double-clicking `Build.bat` (Windows) or running `./Build.sh` (Linux/macOS) launches the interactive setup.

### Running the loader on Linux

`gta6rt.exe` is a Windows binary; on Linux (and macOS under Wine) it cross-compiles with `clang-cl` + `xwin` and runs under Wine or Proton with native Vulkan. See [docs/linux.md](docs/linux.md) and [docs/testing.md](docs/testing.md#the-windows-runtime-on-linux-under-wine-or-proton).

