## Maintainer Notes / Integration Tree

`leonida-ultimate` reconciles verified community PRs and compatible MIT/GPL-3.0 ports onto isolated `blend/*` topic branches with `git cherry` patch-ID deduplication so upstream merges drop out cleanly. Contributors working on Leonida features do **not** need to run any maintainer tooling; if you are curious how upstream PR reconciliation and sanitized local benchmarks work, see [BLENDED.md](BLENDED.md), [ULTIMATE.md](ULTIMATE.md), and [ops/README.md](ops/README.md).

